# What must never reach the public aibrain repo. Its privacy guard (privacy/scan.py, run by git hooks
# and on GitHub) refuses any commit or push whose files, file names, messages or identities contain
# one of these. The guard always catches email addresses, tokens, home folders with a user name,
# tailnet names and private IP addresses; list here what only you know is yours.
#
# One entry per line:
#   word or phrase      matched in any case, as a whole word where it starts or ends with one
#   re:<regex>          a Python regular expression, matched in any case
#   allow:<text>        text that's fine although it contains an entry
#
# Examples (remove the #):
#Your Name
#your-email-name
#my-laptop
#my-secret-project
#re:\bbox\d{2}\b
